For accessing game functions from the appended test code: since `let`/`const` don't attach to global, I need the test code to be in the SAME script. So I'll concatenate: `stubSetup + gameJS + testCode` and run all in one vm context.

Wait — if stubSetup is part of the same script, and it defines `document`, `window`, etc. as `var` or assigns to `globalThis`, then gameJS can access them (as unqualified globals). And the testCode (also in same script) can access gameJS's `let`/`const` vars because they're in the same script scope.

